preConditionHook:
// EL: Highest(high[1], channelBars) / Lowest(low[1], channelBars) -- the window
// ENDS ONE BAR BACK, bars 1..channelBars, so the current bar cannot define the
// level it is being tested against. The shifted series argument makes Extremes
// scan Price[0] .. Price[channelBars - 1], i.e. bars 1..channelBars.
// Extremes is EL SOURCE: seeded on the window's first bar, scanning the rest
// with a strict comparison (a tie keeps the earliest bar) that carries the
// relational tolerance -- hence el_gt/el_lt rather than >/<.
// Same window arithmetic as HighestHighBreakout, but in the EXIT role and
// reaching the OPPOSITE extreme with a tolerance offset: a countertrend short
// covers at the bottom of the channel, a long sells at the top.
// tolerancePoints is in PRICE UNITS -- MinMove / PriceScale are UNKNOWN.
rangeHigh = high[1];
rangeLow = low[1];
for (int i = 2; i <= (int)channelBars; ++i) {
    if (el_gt(high[i], rangeHigh)) rangeHigh = high[i];
    if (el_lt(low[i], rangeLow)) rangeLow = low[i];
}
